      <div class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-2">July 23, 2026 &middot; VPS Provider Review &middot; 14 min read</div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-white mb-4">ServaRica VPS Review 2026: Canadian EPYC KVM from $4/mo</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-400">Canadian operator (Rica Web Services Inc.) on 100% Hydro-Quebec renewable energy. Four AMD EPYC-based product lines, 10Gbps on V3 KVM Slices, full progressive SLA, Alipay + crypto payment stack.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- H2-1 -->
    <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">H2-1: What ServaRica Is and Why It Matters in 2026</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">ServaRica is a Canadian VPS provider operated by Rica Web Services Inc., founded in 2010 by Hani in Montreal, Quebec. The brand emerged from a failed email project (postaRICA): when Hani couldn't find an affordable Canadian-owned host, he bought hardware, co-located it, and built the automation software that became "Xenica." Sixteen years later, ServaRica operates a single Montreal datacenter on 100% Hydro-Quebec renewable energy, with 9 engineers across the team (4 senior system engineers, 1 team lead, 1 founder, plus developer / system engineering support).</p>
      <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">What distinguishes ServaRica from the bulk of the VPS market in 2026 is the combination of <strong>Canadian jurisdiction</strong> (explicitly marketed as outside US Patriot Act / PRISM / Tempora scope), <strong>100% renewable energy</strong> from Hydro-Quebec (99% renewable from water dams), and a <strong>four-product-line structure</strong> that gives the buyer the right shape of VPS for the workload: NVMe VPS for general use, V3 KVM Slices on 10Gbps for high-bandwidth applications, NVMe VDS for dedicated-CPU compute, and Storage Servers on ZFS RAIDZ2 for bulk archival.</p>
      <p class="text-gray-300">For developers who specifically want North American VPS outside US data-residency scope, AMD EPYC compute at budget pricing, and a carbon-conscious operator, ServaRica is the focused pick. For the cheapest possible VPS, <a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">RackNerd's annual-special floor at $10.98/yr across 8 datacenters</a> still wins on price-per-month. For geographic breadth, <a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">Vultr's 32+ global locations</a> or <a href="https://my.racknerd.com/aff.php?aff=16299" class="text-orange-400 hover:underline">LightNode's 40+ locations</a> cover regions ServaRica doesn't reach.</p>
    </div>

    <!-- H2-2 -->
    <div class="bg-[#111] border border-white/5 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-4">H2-2: Verified Pricing &mdash; V3 KVM Slice 2 $4/mo, NVMe Cub $5/mo, Octopus VDS $8/mo</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4">All prices below were live on <code class="bg-gray-800 px-2 py-1 rounded">servarica.com</code> on 2026-07-23, verified via browser_navigate to capture JS-rendered pricing tables (raw curl returns no prices because pricing is loaded via JavaScript).</p>

      <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-orange-400 mb-2">NVMe VPS &mdash; 1Gbps, AMD EPYC, 10 plans</h3>
      <ul class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-6 space-y-1">
        <li>&bull; EPYC - NVMe Cub: 4 GB / 2 vCPU / 12TB / 40 GB NVMe &mdash; <strong>$5/mo</strong> (entry)</li>
        <li>&bull; EPYC - Flying Fish NVMe: 4 GB / 4 vCPU / 12TB / 200 GB NVMe &mdash; <strong>$5/mo</strong> (best entry)</li>
        <li>&bull; EPYC - NVMe Cheetah: 6 GB / 4 vCPU / 12TB / 80 GB NVMe &mdash; $7/mo</li>
        <li>&bull; EPYC - Wildbeest Storage 1: 3 GB / 2 vCPU / 12TB / 250 GB NVMe &mdash; $7/mo</li>
        <li>&bull; EPYC - Swordfish Storage 1: 3 GB / 4 vCPU / 12TB / 400 GB NVMe &mdash; $9/mo</li>
        <li>&bull; EPYC - NVMe Tiger: 10 GB / 4 vCPU / 12TB / 150 GB NVMe &mdash; $10/mo</li>
        <li>&bull; EPYC - Wildbeest Storage 2: 6 GB / 4 vCPU / 24TB / 500 GB NVMe &mdash; $14/mo</li>
        <li>&bull; EPYC - NVMe Cheetah 2: 18 GB / 4 vCPU / 12TB / 240 GB NVMe &mdash; $20/mo</li>
